{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "bbox": [
            0.022,
            0.608,
            0.047,
            0.88
          ],
          "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.083,
            0.883,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": "You would observe that the metal spoon and the metal coin produce a ringing sound. Coal and wood, on the other hand, produce dull sounds."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.141,
            0.883,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": "This property of metals that enables them to produce a ringing sound is called **sonority**, and metals are said to be sonorous in nature."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.08,
            0.197,
            0.25,
            0.364
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.265,
            0.253,
            0.47,
            0.325
          ],
          "content": "Oh! The ringing sound of my ghungroos is also due to the sonority of metals."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.51,
            0.235,
            0.574,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.575,
            0.249,
            0.75,
            0.337
          ],
          "content": "Now, I understand! The ringing sound of the school bell is due to the sonority of metals."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.763,
            0.215,
            0.879,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.377,
            0.579,
            0.399
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "4.1.4 Conduction of heat"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.406,
            0.883,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": "Have you ever observed the vessels used for cooking in the kitchen? You might have noticed that the vessels used for heating are made of metals. Can you name some metals that are used for making cooking vessels? Do you know why these metals are used for this purpose?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.5,
            0.41,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": "Let us find out!"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.274,
            0.534,
            0.578,
            0.554
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 4.3: Let us investigate"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.571,
            0.255,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.571,
            0.884,
            0.607
          ],
          "content": "**Caution**— This activity must be performed under the supervision of your teacher or an adult. Be careful while handling hot water."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.61,
            0.469,
            0.795
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.167,
                0.8,
                0.443,
                0.832
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 4.3: Metal and wooden spoons immersed in hot water"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.487,
            0.61,
            0.832,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": "Place a glass tumbler on a table."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.488,
            0.634,
            0.726,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": "Fill it with hot water."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.488,
            0.659,
            0.883,
            0.715
          ],
          "content": "Take a metal spoon and a wooden spoon of almost the same size and thickness."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.488,
            0.72,
            0.883,
            0.795
          ],
          "content": "Immerse both the spoons simultaneously into the hot water (Fig. 4.3) and leave them undisturbed for a few minutes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.488,
            0.799,
            0.883,
            0.837
          ],
          "content": "Now, carefully touch the upper end of each spoon."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.002,
            0.919,
            0.271,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "",
